 ### [Exponential Depth Cueing](3708-exponential-depth-cueing.md)
-Simulates atmospheric fog by dimming distant voxels using a non-linear transparency falloff based on normalized depth. It sets itself apart from linear cueing by using an exponential function to control how rapidly objects recede, allowing for more natural aerial perspective effects. Choose it when realistic atmospheric depth perception is prioritized over computational simplicity. [Exponential Depth Cueing](3708-exponential-depth-cueing.md)
+Simulates atmospheric fog by dimming distant voxels using a non-linear transparency falloff based on normalized depth. It sets itself apart from linear cueing by using an exponential function to control how rapidly objects recede, allowing for more natural aerial perspective effects. Choose it when realistic atmospheric depth perception is prioritized over computational simplicity.
 
 ### Linear Depth Cueing
-Simulates atmospheric attenuation by blending distant object colors with the background color using a linear interpolation factor based on fragment z-depth relative to maximum scene depth [S9]. It is simpler to implement but may appear less natural than exponential variants for large depth ranges [S9]. Choose it for straightforward depth indication or when linear falloff matches the scene's scale.
