 ## Background
-Originally described as intensity depth-cuing in computer graphics literature [Foley96, cited in S5, unofficial]. It dims distant object colors to simulate viewing through haze [S5]. Adapted for volume rendering to dim sample colors as they recede, augmented with color modulation to increase blue in distant samples, simulating aerial perspective used by painters for centuries [S5][S6, unofficial]. Extended to optical models in volume rendering to enhance depth perception [S8].
